1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,761
For decades,

2
00:00:00,761 --> 00:00:04,061
job interviews have asked one intimidating question:

3
00:00:04,061 --> 00:00:06,599
where do you see yourself in five years?

4
00:00:06,599 --> 00:00:09,454
When tools and whole workflows keep changing,

5
00:00:09,454 --> 00:00:13,135
locking yourself into a rigid five-year script creates two

6
00:00:13,135 --> 00:00:14,530
painful failure modes:

7
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:16,624
endless analysis before starting,

8
00:00:16,624 --> 00:00:20,432
or sunk-cost misery climbing a ladder you outgrew years ago.

9
00:00:20,432 --> 00:00:22,272
In her book Tiny Experiments,

10
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:26,396
neuroscientist Anne-Laure Le Cunff swaps linear life planning for

11
00:00:26,396 --> 00:00:28,046
a more adaptable approach:

12
00:00:28,046 --> 00:00:30,330
treat your career like a laboratory.

13
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:34,432
Traditional goals fail because they anchor your self-worth to

14
00:00:34,432 --> 00:00:36,920
outcomes you cannot directly control,

15
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:40,685
like hitting ten thousand subscribers or landing a dream

16
00:00:40,685 --> 00:00:41,761
title by thirty.

17
00:00:41,761 --> 00:00:43,509
When progress starts slow,

18
00:00:43,509 --> 00:00:45,661
perfectionism tells you to quit.

19
00:00:45,661 --> 00:00:49,494
Le Cunff flips this script with a simple scientific Pact:

20
00:00:49,494 --> 00:00:52,519
I will perform one specific action at a clear

21
00:00:52,519 --> 00:00:53,864
cadence for a short,

22
00:00:53,864 --> 00:00:55,007
bounded duration,

23
00:00:55,007 --> 00:00:58,706
such as publishing one visual insight every morning for

24
00:00:58,706 --> 00:00:59,647
fourteen days,

25
00:00:59,647 --> 00:01:03,412
or building three small automation scripts in two weeks.

26
00:01:03,412 --> 00:01:05,228
During those fourteen days,

27
00:01:05,228 --> 00:01:07,716
you ignore vanity metrics completely.

28
00:01:07,716 --> 00:01:09,531
Success is binary and calm:

29
00:01:09,531 --> 00:01:12,490
did you show up and collect real-world data?

30
00:01:12,490 --> 00:01:16,174
Tiny Experiments become even more powerful when paired with

31
00:01:16,174 --> 00:01:19,607
systems theorist John Gall's nineteen seventy-five law:

32
00:01:19,607 --> 00:01:22,916
every complex system that works evolved from a simple

33
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,477
system that worked first.

34
00:01:24,477 --> 00:01:29,097
Ambitious beginners routinely spend six months in private designing logos,

35
00:01:29,097 --> 00:01:30,034
legal entities,

36
00:01:30,034 --> 00:01:34,029
and forty-page curricula for an audience they have never tested,

37
00:01:34,029 --> 00:01:35,653
only to launch to silence.

38
00:01:35,653 --> 00:01:39,586
A fourteen-day experimental pact forces Version One simplicity.

39
00:01:39,586 --> 00:01:41,396
By shipping ten short essays,

40
00:01:41,396 --> 00:01:42,957
five prototype templates,

41
00:01:42,957 --> 00:01:46,641
or three concise video breakdowns in public over two weeks,

42
00:01:46,641 --> 00:01:50,137
you collect honest market signal for zero dollars before

43
00:01:50,137 --> 00:01:52,010
investing months of your life.

44
00:01:52,010 --> 00:01:54,963
Look closely at many independent creators,

45
00:01:54,963 --> 00:01:55,596
founders,

46
00:01:55,596 --> 00:01:58,619
and analysts and you will notice a pattern:

47
00:01:58,619 --> 00:02:02,135
few of them picked their winning niche on day one.

48
00:02:02,135 --> 00:02:05,228
They ran several small experiments in a row.

49
00:02:05,228 --> 00:02:06,072
For example,

50
00:02:06,072 --> 00:02:08,533
loop one tests productivity habits,

51
00:02:08,533 --> 00:02:10,994
loop two tests visual storytelling,

52
00:02:10,994 --> 00:02:15,283
and loop three combines behavioral economics with dashboards.

53
00:02:15,283 --> 00:02:18,447
One of those angles gets far more replies and

54
00:02:18,447 --> 00:02:19,993
feels easy to produce.

55
00:02:19,993 --> 00:02:23,720
You find that kind of edge through low-stakes contact

56
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:24,634
with reality,

57
00:02:24,634 --> 00:02:26,040
not on a whiteboard.

58
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:28,291
When a fourteen-day pact finishes,

59
00:02:28,291 --> 00:02:31,337
how you review the data determines everything.

60
00:02:31,337 --> 00:02:34,648
Amateurs treat small early numbers as a verdict on

61
00:02:34,648 --> 00:02:35,509
their talent.

62
00:02:35,509 --> 00:02:38,753
Scientists open a single notebook page and run Le

63
00:02:38,753 --> 00:02:41,998
Cunff's ten-minute Plus-Minus-Next retrospective.

64
00:02:41,998 --> 00:02:42,726
Under Plus,

65
00:02:42,726 --> 00:02:46,500
list what gave you energy and resonated with real people.

66
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:47,295
Under Minus,

67
00:02:47,295 --> 00:02:51,069
note the exact bottlenecks that felt unnecessarily heavy.

68
00:02:51,069 --> 00:02:51,797
Under Next,

69
00:02:51,797 --> 00:02:54,975
choose one of three calm paths for the following

70
00:02:54,975 --> 00:02:55,638
two weeks:

71
00:02:55,638 --> 00:02:57,756
Persist if momentum is building,

72
00:02:57,756 --> 00:03:00,604
Pivot one variable such as format or topic,

73
00:03:00,604 --> 00:03:05,040
or consciously Pause the experiment guilt-free with lessons banked.

74
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:08,248
Retire the pressure of figuring out the next five

75
00:03:08,248 --> 00:03:12,243
years and design one fourteen-day Tiny Experiment today using

76
00:03:12,243 --> 00:03:13,028
three rules.

77
00:03:13,028 --> 00:03:13,618
Rule one:

78
00:03:13,618 --> 00:03:16,106
write a single concrete pact sentence,

79
00:03:16,106 --> 00:03:16,891
for example,

80
00:03:16,891 --> 00:03:21,016
I will publish one three-hundred-word mental model breakdown or

81
00:03:21,016 --> 00:03:24,683
build one useful spreadsheet template every two days for

82
00:03:24,683 --> 00:03:25,600
fourteen days.

83
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:26,189
Rule two:

84
00:03:26,189 --> 00:03:29,790
cap daily execution under forty-five minutes so you can

85
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:32,737
complete every rep alongside a full-time job.

86
00:03:32,737 --> 00:03:33,457
Rule three:

87
00:03:33,457 --> 00:03:36,797
refuse to judge metrics until day fourteen arrives,

88
00:03:36,797 --> 00:03:39,219
then run your Plus-Minus-Next review.

89
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,791
Six tiny loops from now,

90
00:03:40,791 --> 00:03:44,130
your skills and direction will look unrecognizable.
